    "#ScienceForKids"
  ],
  "tags": [
    "butterfly life cycle for kids",
    "caterpillar to butterfly",
    "metamorphosis for kids",
    "chrysalis",
    "animal facts",
    "science for kids",
    "kids learning"
  ],
  "cast": [
    "LEO",
    "MIA"
  ],
  "loop_card": {
    "text": "Caterpillar to butterfly?",
    "cue": "next",
    "left": "🐛",
    "right": "🦋"
  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, how does a crawly caterpillar turn into a butterfly with wings?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "🐛",
          "label": "Caterpillar"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "🦋",
          "label": "Butterfly"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It's one of the biggest changes in nature! Today we'll follow one tiny egg all the way to a butterfly.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "✨",
        "text": "The biggest change!",
        "cue": "biggest",
        "sub": "From egg to wings",
        "sub_cue": "egg"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Wait, it starts as an egg?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yep! And this change has a special name: metamorphosis. It means a big change in shape.",
      "punch": "metamorphosis",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔄",
        "text": "Metamorphosis",
        "cue": "metamorphosis",
        "sub": "A big change in shape",
        "sub_cue": "shape"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Meta-mor-pho-sis. Got it! Let's go!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "First, a mother butterfly looks for just the right plant. She tastes the leaves with her feet!",
      "chapter": "A tiny egg",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🦋",
        "text": "Find the right plant",
        "cue": "plant",
        "sub": "Taste with feet!",
        "sub_cue": "feet"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "With her feet? That's so silly!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Then she lays tiny eggs, often under a leaf, where they stay hidden. Each egg is about as small as a pinhead!",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Egg time",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🥚",
            "label": "Tiny eggs",
            "cue": "eggs"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🍃",
            "label": "Under a leaf",
            "cue": "under"
          },
          {
            "icon": "📌",
            "label": "Pinhead small",
            "cue": "pinhead"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And what comes out of the egg?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "A teeny caterpillar! And guess what its very first meal often is? Its own eggshell!",
      "punch": "eggshell",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🥚",
        "text": "First snack: eggshell!",
        "cue": "eggshell"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Then what does it eat?",
      "chapter": "Hungry caterpillar"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Leaves, leaves and more leaves! A caterpillar is like a tiny eating machine. Its main job is to eat and grow.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🍃",
        "text": "A tiny eating machine",
        "cue": "machine",
        "sub": "Eat and grow!",
        "sub_cue": "grow"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "That sounds like the best job ever!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Each kind of caterpillar likes its own plants. Monarch caterpillars only eat milkweed leaves.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌿",
        "text": "Each kind, its own plant",
        "cue": "kind",
        "sub": "Monarchs: milkweed",
        "sub_cue": "milkweed"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "But if it eats so much, won't its skin get too tight?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Great thinking! Its skin can't stretch forever. So it wriggles out of its old skin, and there's a new, bigger skin underneath.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "Growing up",
        "traveler": "🐛",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "👕",
            "label": "Tight skin",
            "cue": "skin"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌀",
            "label": "Wriggle out",
            "cue": "wriggles"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✨",
            "label": "Bigger skin",
            "cue": "bigger"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Like taking off a sweater that's too small!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Exactly! It does this a few times, and each time it gets bigger and bigger.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "📏",
        "text": "A few new skins",
        "cue": "few",
        "sub": "Bigger and bigger!",
        "sub_cue": "bigger"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And when it's big enough?",
      "chapter": "The chrysalis"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It finds a safe spot and hangs upside down, often in a little J shape.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🙃",
        "text": "Hang upside down",
        "cue": "hangs",
        "sub": "Like a letter J",
        "sub_cue": "j"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Is it doing a trick?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Kind of! Its skin splits one last time, and underneath is a hard, shiny case. That case is called a chrysalis.",
      "punch": "chrysalis",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎁",
        "text": "A hard, shiny case",
        "cue": "hard",
        "sub": "Called a chrysalis",
        "sub_cue": "chrysalis"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Is that the same as a cocoon?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Not quite! Moth caterpillars usually spin a cocoon out of silk. Butterflies make a chrysalis from their own skin.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Moths",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🧶",
              "text": "Silk cocoon",
              "cue": "cocoon"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Butterflies",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🎁",
              "text": "Chrysalis",
              "cue": "chrysalis"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So what's happening in there? Is it sleeping?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It looks still, but inside it's super busy! Much of the caterpillar's body breaks down into a kind of goo.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌀",
        "text": "Super busy inside!",
        "cue": "busy",
        "sub": "Turns into goo",
        "sub_cue": "goo"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Goo?! Then how does it become a butterfly?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Some special groups of cells were waiting inside all along. They use the goo like building blocks to make a brand-new body.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧱",
        "text": "Building blocks",
        "cue": "building",
        "sub": "A brand-new body",
        "sub_cue": "brand"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What does it build?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Wings, long legs, big eyes, and a long, curly tongue for sipping.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Brand-new parts",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🦋",
            "label": "Wings",
            "cue": "wings"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🦵",
            "label": "Long legs",
            "cue": "legs"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👀",
            "label": "Big eyes",
            "cue": "eyes"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👅",
            "label": "Curly tongue",
            "cue": "tongue"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How long does it stay in there?",
      "chapter": "Hello, butterfly!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "For many butterflies, about one or two weeks. Then the chrysalis cracks open, and out comes a butterfly!",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Coming out",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🐣",
            "label": "The case cracks open",
            "cue": "cracks"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🦋",
            "label": "Out comes a butterfly",
            "cue": "out"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Can it fly right away?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Not yet! Its wings are soft and crumpled. It pumps fluid into them, then waits for them to dry and harden.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Getting ready",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🦋",
            "label": "Soft, crumpled wings",
            "cue": "soft"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💧",
            "label": "Pump them up",
            "cue": "pumps"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌬️",
            "label": "Dry and harden",
            "cue": "dry"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And then... whoosh?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Then off it flies! Now it drinks sweet nectar from flowers, using its tongue like a straw.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌸",
        "text": "Sipping nectar",
        "cue": "nectar",
        "sub": "Tongue like a straw",
        "sub_cue": "straw"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "A butterfly with a built-in straw!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Later, she lays her own eggs. Each egg hatches into a caterpillar, which makes a chrysalis, which turns into a butterfly. Round and round: a life cycle!",
      "board": {
        "type": "cycle",
        "title": "Butterfly life cycle",
        "center": "🌿",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🥚",
            "label": "Egg",
            "cue": "eggs"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🐛",
            "label": "Caterpillar",
            "cue": "caterpillar"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🎁",
            "label": "Chrysalis",
            "cue": "chrysalis"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🦋",
            "label": "Butterfly",
            "cue": "butterfly"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Round and round, like a merry-go-round!"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Quiz time! Question one: what is a caterpillar's very first meal, most of the time? Think...",
      "chapter": "Quiz time",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❓",
        "text": "Quiz time!",
        "cue": "quiz",
        "sub": "First meal?",
        "sub_cue": "first"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Its own eggshell!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🥚",
        "text": "Its eggshell!",
        "cue": "eggshell"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Question two: what's the hard case called, where the caterpillar changes? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🤔",
        "text": "What's the case called?",
        "cue": "case"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "A chrysalis!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎁",
        "text": "Chrysalis!",
        "cue": "chrysalis"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Right! Last one: how does a butterfly taste a leaf? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🍃",
        "text": "How does it taste?",
        "cue": "taste"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "With its feet! Still so silly!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🦶",
        "text": "With its feet!",
        "cue": "feet"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Brilliant! So, a tiny egg hatches, the caterpillar eats and grows, the chrysalis rebuilds its body, and a butterfly flies away.",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "icon": "🥚",
            "text": "Egg hatches",
            "cue": "egg"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🐛",
            "text": "Eat and grow",
            "cue": "eats"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🎁",
            "text": "Chrysalis rebuilds",
            "cue": "chrysalis"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🦋",
            "text": "Butterfly flies!",
            "cue": "butterfly"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Metamorphosis! The biggest change in nature!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "✨",
        "text": "Metamorphosis!",
        "cue": "metamorphosis"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Next time you see a butterfly, remember it was once a caterpillar! Ask a grown-up to subscribe to The Curio Kids Club for more wonders! And next time someone asks... how does a caterpillar become a butterfly?"
    }
  ]
}
